<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="es">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Memoria Técnica Interactiva - ACI 318</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js"></script>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
        body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }
        .chart-container {
            position: relative;
            width: 100%;
            max-width: 700px;
            margin-left: auto;
            margin-right: auto;
            height: 350px;
            max-height: 400px;
        }
        .canvas-container {
            position: relative;
            width: 100%;
            max-width: 400px;
            margin-left: auto;
            margin-right: auto;
            height: 400px;
        }
        .view-section { display: none; }
        .view-section.active { display: block; animation: fadeIn 0.4s; }
        @keyframes fadeIn { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); } }
        .math-block { background-color: #f8fafc; border-left: 4px solid #0284c7; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 0.25rem; font-family: monospace; font-size: 1.1rem; }
    </style>
</head>
<body class="bg-stone-50 text-stone-800 flex flex-col md:flex-row min-h-screen">

    <!-- Chosen Palette: Warm Neutrals with Sky Blue Accents (bg-stone-50, text-stone-800, border-stone-200, bg-sky-600 for actions, bg-sky-50 for highlights) -->
    
    <!-- Application Structure Plan: A dashboard-style layout with a fixed sidebar for navigation and a main content area. This structure allows users to logically step through the theoretical concepts (Hypotheses -> Parameters -> Procedure -> Factors) without being overwhelmed by a massive wall of text. Interactive elements (sliders and dynamic charts) are placed immediately alongside the corresponding theory to reinforce learning through exploration. -->
    
    <!-- Visualization & Content Choices: 
         - Material Parameters (Beta1): Line chart (Chart.js) + Slider. Goal: Show the step-wise function of Beta1 based on f'c. Justification: Visualizing the plateau and slope helps understand the ACI 318 rule instantly.
         - Strain Compatibility: HTML5 Canvas drawing + Slider. Goal: Illustrate how varying the neutral axis depth (c) changes the strain in steel. Justification: A geometric representation of "plane sections remain plane" is the most effective way to teach strain compatibility. NO SVG used.
         - Phi Factors: Line chart (Chart.js). Goal: Show the transition of the reduction factor. Justification: The piecewise function is best understood visually. 
    -->
    
    <!-- CONFIRMATION: NO SVG graphics used. NO Mermaid JS used. -->

    <nav class="w-full md:w-64 bg-stone-900 text-stone-100 flex-shrink-0 flex flex-col shadow-xl z-10 sticky top-0 md:h-screen">
        <div class="p-6 border-b border-stone-800">
            <h1 class="text-xl font-bold text-sky-400 tracking-tight">Memoria ACI 318</h1>
            <p class="text-xs text-stone-400 mt-1 uppercase tracking-widest">Análisis Interactivo</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex-grow overflow-y-auto py-4 flex flex-col gap-1 px-3">
            <button class="nav-btn text-left px-4 py-3 rounded-lg transition-colors bg-sky-600 text-white font-semibold" data-target="hipotesis">1. Hipótesis de Diseño</button>
            <button class="nav-btn text-left px-4 py-3 rounded-lg transition-colors hover:bg-stone-800 text-stone-300" data-target="parametros">2. Parámetros (&#946;&#8321;)</button>
            <button class="nav-btn text-left px-4 py-3 rounded-lg transition-colors hover:bg-stone-800 text-stone-300" data-target="procedimiento">3. Procedimiento y Esfuerzos</button>
            <button class="nav-btn text-left px-4 py-3 rounded-lg transition-colors hover:bg-stone-800 text-stone-300" data-target="factores">4. Puntos Singulares y Factor &#981;</button>
        </div>
    </nav>

    <main class="flex-grow p-6 md:p-12 overflow-y-auto w-full">
        
        <section id="hipotesis" class="view-section active max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4 border-b pb-2 border-stone-200">1. Hipótesis de Diseño</h2>
            <p class="text-stone-600 mb-8 text-lg leading-relaxed">
                Esta sección establece los fundamentos teóricos para el diseño por resistencia de columnas de concreto armado. Aquí se presentan las reglas básicas que rigen el comportamiento conjunto del acero y el concreto, esenciales para comprender el resto de la memoria de cálculo.
            </p>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-stone-200 hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
                    <div class="text-2xl mb-2">&#128207;</div>
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-sky-700 mb-2">Compatibilidad de Deformaciones</h3>
                    <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm">Las deformaciones en el acero y el concreto son directamente proporcionales a su distancia al eje neutro. Esto significa que las secciones planas antes de la flexión permanecen planas después de la flexión.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-stone-200 hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
                    <div class="text-2xl mb-2">&#129704;</div>
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-sky-700 mb-2">Resistencia del Concreto</h3>
                    <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm">Se asume que la falla del concreto ocurre cuando la fibra extrema sometida a compresión alcanza una deformación máxima útil definida normativamente como <strong>&#949;<sub>u</sub> = 0.003</strong>.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-stone-200 hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
                    <div class="text-2xl mb-2">&#9875;</div>
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-sky-700 mb-2">Esfuerzo del Acero</h3>
                    <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm">El esfuerzo se calcula mediante la Ley de Hooke (f<sub>s</sub> = E<sub>s</sub> &middot; &#949;<sub>s</sub>), limitándose al esfuerzo de fluencia (f<sub>y</sub>). El módulo de elasticidad es <strong>E<sub>s</sub> = 2,000,000 kg/cm&sup2;</strong>.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-stone-200 hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
                    <div class="text-2xl mb-2">&#128306;</div>
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-sky-700 mb-2">Bloque de Whitney</h3>
                    <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm">Para simplificar el cálculo manual y analítico, la distribución parabólica real de esfuerzos de compresión en el concreto se reemplaza por un bloque rectangular equivalente de tensiones.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="parametros" class="view-section max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4 border-b pb-2 border-stone-200">2. Parámetros del Material (Bloque &#946;&#8321;)</h2>
            <p class="text-stone-600 mb-8 text-lg leading-relaxed">
                El factor &#946;&#8321; es crucial para definir la profundidad del bloque rectangular equivalente de compresión (a = &#946;&#8321; &middot; c). En esta sección interactiva, puedes explorar cómo la resistencia a la compresión del concreto (f'c) altera este parámetro normativo.
            </p>

            <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-stone-200 mb-8">
                <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 items-center">
                    <div class="w-full md:w-1/3 space-y-6">
                        <div>
                            <label class="block text-sm font-bold text-stone-500 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Ajustar Resistencia f'c (kg/cm&sup2;)</label>
                            <input type="range" id="fcSlider" min="150" max="700" step="10" value="210" class="w-full h-2 bg-stone-200 rounded-lg appearance-none cursor-pointer accent-sky-600">
                            <div class="mt-4 text-center">
                                <span class="text-4xl font-black text-stone-800" id="fcValDisplay">210</span>
                                <span class="text-stone-500">kg/cm&sup2;</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="bg-sky-50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-sky-100 text-center">
                            <span class="block text-xs font-bold text-sky-600 uppercase mb-1">Factor Calculado &#946;&#8321;</span>
                            <span class="text-3xl font-black text-sky-800" id="betaValDisplay">0.850</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="w-full md:w-2/3">
                        <div class="chart-container">
                            <canvas id="betaChart"></canvas>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="mt-6 math-block text-sm">
                    Si f'c &le; 280 &rArr; &#946;&#8321; = 0.85 <br>
                    Si f'c &ge; 560 &rArr; &#946;&#8321; = 0.65 <br>
                    Intermedios: &#946;&#8321; = 0.85 - [0.05 &middot; (f'c - 280) / 70]
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="procedimiento" class="view-section max-w-5xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4 border-b pb-2 border-stone-200">3. Procedimiento y Compatibilidad</h2>
            <p class="text-stone-600 mb-8 text-lg leading-relaxed">
                El corazón de la iteración para el diagrama es el análisis de compatibilidad de deformaciones. Al variar la profundidad del eje neutro (c), cambian las deformaciones en el acero y el concreto, lo que a su vez modifica las fuerzas internas de la sección.
            </p>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-8">
                <div class="space-y-6">
                    <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-stone-200">
                        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-800 mb-3 border-b pb-2">A. Deformaciones y Esfuerzos</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 mb-3">Para cada capa de acero ubicada a una profundidad d<sub>i</sub>, la deformación se obtiene por semejanza de triángulos:</p>
                        <div class="math-block mb-3">&#949;<sub>si</sub> = 0.003 &middot; (c - d<sub>i</sub>) / c</div>
                        <div class="math-block">f<sub>si</sub> = max(-f<sub>y</sub>, min(f<sub>y</sub>, E<sub>s</sub> &middot; &#949;<sub>si</sub>))</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-stone-200">
                        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-800 mb-3 border-b pb-2">B. Equilibrio Interno</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 mb-3">Las fuerzas internas definen la carga axial (P<sub>n</sub>) y el momento flector (M<sub>n</sub>) resistente:</p>
                        <div class="math-block mb-3">
                            Compresión Concreto: C<sub>c</sub> = 0.85 &middot; f'c &middot; b &middot; a
                        </div>
                        <div class="math-block mb-3">
                            Carga Axial: P<sub>n</sub> = C<sub>c</sub> + &Sigma; (A<sub>si</sub> &middot; f<sub>si</sub>)
                        </div>
                        <div class="math-block text-xs">
                            Momento: M<sub>n</sub> = C<sub>c</sub> &middot; (h/2 - a/2) + &Sigma; [A<sub>si</sub> &middot; f<sub>si</sub> &middot; (h/2 - d<sub>i</sub>)]
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-stone-800 p-6 rounded-2xl shadow-lg text-white flex flex-col items-center">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-sky-400 mb-4 w-full text-center uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">Simulador de Eje Neutro</h3>
                    <div class="w-full px-4 mb-6">
                        <label class="block text-xs font-bold text-stone-400 mb-2">Profundidad Eje Neutro (c) = <span id="cValDisplay" class="text-white text-lg">25</span> cm</label>
                        <input type="range" id="cSlider" min="5" max="60" step="1" value="25" class="w-full h-2 bg-stone-600 rounded-lg appearance-none cursor-pointer accent-sky-400">
                    </div>
                    <div class="canvas-container bg-stone-900 rounded-xl border border-stone-700 overflow-hidden">
                        <canvas id="strainCanvas" width="400" height="400"></canvas>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-[10px] text-stone-400 mt-4 text-center px-4">Representación visual de la deformación unitaria (&#949;). Note cómo el acero inferior pasa de tracción a compresión al aumentar 'c'. Sección asumida: h=60cm, d=54cm.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="factores" class="view-section max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-4 border-b pb-2 border-stone-200">4. Puntos Singulares y Resistencia de Diseño</h2>
            <p class="text-stone-600 mb-8 text-lg leading-relaxed">
                El diagrama final depende de condiciones críticas (compresión pura, falla balanceada) y de la aplicación de factores de reducción de resistencia (&#981;) dictados por la norma, los cuales penalizan secciones que fallan frágilmente.
            </p>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-8">
                <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-stone-200">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-sky-700 mb-2 text-lg">Compresión Pura (P<sub>0</sub>)</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 mb-3">Es la capacidad axial máxima de la columna cuando la excentricidad es nula.</p>
                    <div class="math-block text-sm">P<sub>0</sub> = 0.85 &middot; f'c &middot; (A<sub>g</sub> - A<sub>st</sub>) + A<sub>st</sub> &middot; f<sub>y</sub></div>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-stone-200">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-sky-700 mb-2 text-lg">Falla Balanceada (c<sub>bal</sub>)</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 mb-3">Ocurre simultáneamente el aplastamiento del concreto (&#949;=0.003) y la fluencia del acero extremo.</p>
                    <div class="math-block text-sm">c<sub>bal</sub> = [0.003 / (0.003 + f<sub>y</sub>/E<sub>s</sub>)] &middot; d<sub>ext</sub></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-stone-200">
                <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-800 mb-4 text-xl">Factor de Reducción &#981; (ACI 318)</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 mb-6">El factor &#981; se calcula en función de la deformación neta de tracción (&#949;<sub>t</sub>) en la capa extrema de acero. Valores bajos de deformación indican falla por compresión (frágil, &#981;=0.65), mientras que valores altos indican falla por flexión (dúctil, &#981;=0.90).</p>
                
                <div class="chart-container mb-6">
                    <canvas id="phiChart"></canvas>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 p-4 rounded-lg">
                    <strong class="text-amber-800 text-sm block mb-1">Verificación de Seguridad y Límite Máximo</strong>
                    <p class="text-xs text-amber-700">Por normatividad ante excentricidades accidentales, la carga máxima de diseño se trunca horizontalmente en el diagrama a un valor de <strong>&#981;P<sub>n,max</sub> = 0.80 &middot; &#981; &middot; P<sub>0</sub></strong> (para columnas con estribos). Un diseño es seguro si la carga solicitante (M<sub>u</sub>, P<sub>u</sub>) cae dentro del área delimitada por esta curva ajustada.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

    </main>

    <script>
        const state = {
            fc: 210,
            fy: 4200,
            es: 2000000,
            cVal: 25,
            h: 60,
            d: 54 
        };

        const elements = {
            navBtns: document.querySelectorAll('.nav-btn'),
            sections: document.querySelectorAll('.view-section'),
            fcSlider: document.getElementById('fcSlider'),
            fcValDisplay: document.getElementById('fcValDisplay'),
            betaValDisplay: document.getElementById('betaValDisplay'),
            cSlider: document.getElementById('cSlider'),
            cValDisplay: document.getElementById('cValDisplay'),
            betaCanvas: document.getElementById('betaChart'),
            phiCanvas: document.getElementById('phiChart'),
            strainCanvas: document.getElementById('strainCanvas')
        };

        let betaChartInst = null;
        let phiChartInst = null;

        function initNav() {
            elements.navBtns.forEach(btn => {
                btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
                    elements.navBtns.forEach(b => {
                        b.classList.remove('bg-sky-600', 'text-white', 'font-semibold');
                        b.classList.add('hover:bg-stone-800', 'text-stone-300');
                    });
                    btn.classList.remove('hover:bg-stone-800', 'text-stone-300');
                    btn.classList.add('bg-sky-600', 'text-white', 'font-semibold');

                    const targetId = btn.getAttribute('data-target');
                    elements.sections.forEach(sec => sec.classList.remove('active'));
                    document.getElementById(targetId).classList.add('active');
                    
                    if(targetId === 'factores') updatePhiChart();
                });
            });
        }

        function calcBeta1(fc) {
            if (fc <= 280) return 0.85;
            if (fc >= 560) return 0.65;
            return 0.85 - (0.05 * (fc - 280) / 70);
        }

        function initBetaChart() {
            const dataPts = [];
            for(let i=150; i<=700; i+=10) {
                dataPts.push({x: i, y: calcBeta1(i)});
            }

            betaChartInst = new Chart(elements.betaCanvas, {
                type: 'line',
                data: {
                    datasets: [{
                        label: 'Valor de β1',
                        data: dataPts,
                        borderColor: '#94a3b8',
                        borderWidth: 2,
                        pointRadius: 0,
                        fill: false,
                        tension: 0
                    }, {
                        label: 'Selección Actual',
                        data: [{x: state.fc, y: calcBeta1(state.fc)}],
                        backgroundColor: '#0284c7',
                        borderColor: '#fff',
                        borderWidth: 2,
                        pointRadius: 8,
                        pointHoverRadius: 10
                    }]
                },
                options: {
                    responsive: true,
                    maintainAspectRatio: false,
                    scales: {
                        x: { title: { display: true, text: "Resistencia f'c (kg/cm²)" }, type: 'linear', min: 150, max: 700 },
                        y: { title: { display: true, text: 'Factor β1' }, min: 0.60, max: 0.90 }
                    },
                    plugins: { legend: { display: false } }
                }
            });
        }

        function updateBetaSection() {
            state.fc = parseInt(elements.fcSlider.value);
            const beta = calcBeta1(state.fc);
            
            elements.fcValDisplay.textContent = state.fc;
            elements.betaValDisplay.textContent = beta.toFixed(3);

            if(betaChartInst) {
                betaChartInst.data.datasets[1].data = [{x: state.fc, y: beta}];
                betaChartInst.update();
            }
        }

        function drawStrainProfile() {
            const ctx = elements.strainCanvas.getContext('2d');
            const w = elements.strainCanvas.width;
            const h = elements.strainCanvas.height;
            
            ctx.clearRect(0, 0, w, h);

            const pad = 40;
            const colW = 80;
            const colH = h - 2*pad;
            const colX = pad;
            const colY = pad;

            const ey = state.fy / state.es; 
            const realC = state.cVal; 
            const ratio = colH / state.h; 
            const drawC = realC * ratio;
            const drawD = state.d * ratio;

            ctx.fillStyle = '#292524';
            ctx.fillRect(colX, colY, colW, colH);
            
            ctx.fillStyle = '#44403c';
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.arc(colX + 20, colY + 20, 5, 0, Math.PI*2);
            ctx.arc(colX + colW - 20, colY + 20, 5, 0, Math.PI*2);
            ctx.fill();
            
            ctx.fillStyle = '#38bdf8'; 
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.arc(colX + 20, colY + drawD, 5, 0, Math.PI*2);
            ctx.arc(colX + colW - 20, colY + drawD, 5, 0, Math.PI*2);
            ctx.fill();

            const naY = colY + drawC;
            ctx.strokeStyle = '#a8a29e';
            ctx.setLineDash([5, 5]);
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.moveTo(colX - 10, naY);
            ctx.lineTo(w - pad, naY);
            ctx.stroke();
            ctx.setLineDash([]);

            ctx.fillStyle = '#a8a29e';
            ctx.font = '12px Inter';
            ctx.fillText('Eje Neutro (c)', w - pad - 80, naY - 5);

            const strainAxisX = colX + colW + 60;
            ctx.strokeStyle = '#57534e';
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.moveTo(strainAxisX, colY);
            ctx.lineTo(strainAxisX, colY + colH);
            ctx.stroke();

            const maxStrainW = 80; 
            const concStrainX = strainAxisX + maxStrainW; 
            
            ctx.strokeStyle = '#38bdf8';
            ctx.lineWidth = 2;
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.moveTo(concStrainX, colY); 
            
            const realStrainSteel = 0.003 * (realC - state.d) / realC;
            
            const steelStrainX = strainAxisX + (realStrainSteel / 0.003) * maxStrainW;

            ctx.lineTo(strainAxisX, naY);
            ctx.lineTo(steelStrainX, colY + drawD);
            ctx.stroke();

            ctx.fillStyle = '#38bdf8';
            ctx.fillText('ε_c = 0.003', concStrainX + 5, colY + 10);
            
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.moveTo(strainAxisX, colY);
            ctx.lineTo(concStrainX, colY);
            ctx.stroke();
            
            ctx.beginPath();
            ctx.moveTo(strainAxisX, colY + drawD);
            ctx.lineTo(steelStrainX, colY + drawD);
            ctx.stroke();

            ctx.fillText(`ε_s = ${realStrainSteel.toFixed(4)}`, steelStrainX + (realStrainSteel > 0 ? 5 : -70), colY + drawD + (realStrainSteel > 0 ? 15 : -5));
        }

        function updateStrainSection() {
            state.cVal = parseInt(elements.cSlider.value);
            elements.cValDisplay.textContent = state.cVal;
            drawStrainProfile();
        }

        function calcPhi(et, ey) {
            if (et <= ey) return 0.65;
            if (et >= 0.005) return 0.90;
            return 0.65 + 0.25 * ((et - ey) / (0.005 - ey));
        }

        function updatePhiChart() {
            if(!phiChartInst) {
                const ey = state.fy / state.es;
                const dataPts = [];
                for(let et=0; et<=0.008; et+=0.0001) {
                    dataPts.push({x: et, y: calcPhi(et, ey)});
                }

                phiChartInst = new Chart(elements.phiCanvas, {
                    type: 'line',
                    data: {
                        datasets: [{
                            label: 'Factor φ',
                            data: dataPts,
                            borderColor: '#0284c7',
                            borderWidth: 3,
                            pointRadius: 0,
                            fill: true,
                            backgroundColor: 'rgba(2, 132, 199, 0.1)'
                        }]
                    },
                    options: {
                        responsive: true,
                        maintainAspectRatio: false,
                        scales: {
                            x: { 
                                title: { display: true, text: "Deformación neta de tracción (ε_t)" }, 
                                type: 'linear', 
                                min: 0, 
                                max: 0.008,
                                grid: { color: '#f5f5f4' }
                            },
                            y: { 
                                title: { display: true, text: 'Factor de Reducción φ' }, 
                                min: 0.5, 
                                max: 1.0,
                                grid: { color: '#f5f5f4' }
                            }
                        },
                        plugins: { 
                            legend: { display: false },
                            tooltip: {
                                callbacks: { label: (ctx) => `φ = ${ctx.parsed.y.toFixed(3)}` }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                });
            }
        }

        elements.fcSlider.addEventListener('input', updateBetaSection);
        elements.cSlider.addEventListener('input', updateStrainSection);

        window.onload = () => {
            initNav();
            initBetaChart();
            updateBetaSection();
            updateStrainSection();
        };

    </script>
</body>
</html>
